WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Two students answer the same
4-mark question about pacifism.

2
00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:06.810
Both make the same two points.

3
00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:08.880
Both points are accurate.

4
00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:12.270
Yet one answer scores far
more marks than the other.

5
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:15.520
If the points are the same,
what makes the difference?

6
00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:19.280
In this mission, you'll take
apart a question in five parts,

7
00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:22.000
from 1 mark all the way up to 12.

8
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:25.310
Then you'll test which
sentences really earn marks,

9
00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:27.560
and which only look as if they do.

10
00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:33.150
Your mission: find out why two answers with
the same points can score so differently.
